{"id":"eead54fba77071123c7c3c2252c6e181213a5f97","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"eead54fba77071123c7c3c2252c6e181213a5f97","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/global-virtual-store-by-default.md","lines":["@@ -1,13 +0,0 @@","-\"pacquet\": major","-","-The global virtual store is now enabled by default. A package is materialized under `<store-dir>/v11/links/` once per machine for each distinct set of dependencies it resolves to, and shared by every project that resolves it the same way, instead of being re-created inside each project's `node_modules/.pnpm`. Installing a dependency another project already installed the same way is close to free, and those projects no longer pay for it twice on disk.","-","-The default is the same in every environment, CI included, so a build never runs against a layout nobody develops against. To opt out, set the setting in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`:","-","-```yaml","-enableGlobalVirtualStore: false","-```","-","-Because the package directories now live outside the project, a dependency's own dependencies are reachable through symlinks and `NODE_PATH` rather than by walking up the filesystem from a package's real path. Tools that resolve modules by walking directories themselves, instead of asking Node.js to resolve them, may not find a dependency they used to find. Turning the setting off restores the project-local layout."],"additions":0,"deletions":11,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/src/config_deps/tests.rs","lines":["@@ -105,11 +105,7 @@ async fn update_config_can_extend_extra_bin_paths() {"," #[tokio::test]"," async fn update_config_can_set_extra_env() {","     let root = tempfile::tempdir().expect(\"workspace tempdir\");","-    // The shared virtual store seeds `extraEnv` with the `NODE_PATH` /","-    // `NODE_OPTIONS` pair that makes hoisted dependencies resolvable, so","-    // turn it off to start the hook from an empty map.","-    fs::write(root.path().join(\"pnpm-workspace.yaml\"), \"enableGlobalVirtualS